<p align="left"><span class="style29"></span><small><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">The Conference for Undergraduate Women in Physics at Yale (CUPWY) is a
three-day conference for undergraduate physics majors in the
northeastern United States.&nbsp; The University of Southern California
(USC) and the University of Michigan (UMich) will be holding similar
conferences concurrently, and all these conferences will be based on
two very successful conferences that USC held in 2006 and 2007.&nbsp; Our
goal is to help young women continue in physics by providing them with
information about graduate school and professions in physics, allowing
them the opportunity to experience a professional conference, and
giving them access to other women in physics of all ages with whom they
can share experiences, advice, and ideas.&nbsp; Our schedule includes
research talks by faculty, panel discussions about graduate school and
careers in physics, presentations and discussions about women in
physics, laboratory tours, student research talks, a student poster
session, and several meals during which presenters and students can
interact with each other.
